VALUES ('bcc754bf-d1f5-43c2-9a6c-2950b40639f3', 'rhce-navigator-collections-ee', 'RHCE Ansible Practice: Content Collections, Execution Environments & ansible-navigator', 'ansible', ARRAY['RHCE', 'EX294', 'ansible-navigator', 'Execution Environments', 'Content Collections', 'ansible-builder']::TEXT[], 38, 'advanced', true, 5, 60, 1, 0);

-- ── Section: Content Collections & ansible-galaxy (9 questions) — Ansible Content Collections — FQCNs, ansible-galaxy collection install, requirements.yml — authored from docs.ansible.com's collections user guide; verified via web search 2026-09-04. ──

VALUES ('451f1e9c-e504-4318-b409-06a0ce04956b', 'bcc754bf-d1f5-43c2-9a6c-2950b40639f3', 1, 'A Fully Qualified Collection Name (FQCN) used to reference a module in a playbook has the form:', 'Ansible', 'FQCN Format', 'mcq');
VALUES ('451f1e9c-e504-4318-b409-06a0ce04956b', '93850c8d-93f1-43ab-9baf-df7cd1a0f7d6', 'An FQCN is three dot-separated parts: namespace.collection.content — e.g. ansible.posix.firewalld or community.general.ufw.', 'Ansible Content Collections — FQCNs, ansible-galaxy collection install, requirements.yml — authored from docs.ansible.com''s collections user guide; verified via web search 2026-09-04.');

VALUES ('17e61b54-6523-41b3-b52a-35bb01a35a2c', 'bcc754bf-d1f5-43c2-9a6c-2950b40639f3', 2, 'Why does Red Hat''s RHCE curriculum and Ansible''s own best-practice guidance recommend always using FQCNs for module names in playbooks, rather than short names like `firewalld`?', 'Ansible', 'Why Use FQCNs', 'mcq');
VALUES ('17e61b54-6523-41b3-b52a-35bb01a35a2c', '4e1dc67c-5231-4979-9a57-c0f8ebb715ed', 'Multiple collections can ship modules with identical short names; the FQCN disambiguates which collection''s implementation is used and documents the collection dependency directly in the playbook.', 'Ansible Content Collections — FQCNs, ansible-galaxy collection install, requirements.yml — authored from docs.ansible.com''s collections user guide; verified via web search 2026-09-04.');

VALUES ('d56b555f-db52-478f-bd56-959c08ef7183', 'bcc754bf-d1f5-43c2-9a6c-2950b40639f3', 3, 'What does `ansible-galaxy collection install community.general` do if no version or path is specified?', 'Ansible', 'ansible-galaxy collection install', 'mcq');
VALUES ('d56b555f-db52-478f-bd56-959c08ef7183', 'f092dc81-a5fc-474a-9876-e6a19afa9f4a', 'Without a version constraint, ansible-galaxy installs the latest available version; without -p, it installs to the first entry in COLLECTIONS_PATHS, which defaults to ~/.ansible/collections.', 'Ansible Content Collections — FQCNs, ansible-galaxy collection install, requirements.yml — authored from docs.ansible.com''s collections user guide; verified via web search 2026-09-04.');

VALUES ('a38913a7-ef13-43cc-a508-23cf981d9986', 'bcc754bf-d1f5-43c2-9a6c-2950b40639f3', 4, 'In `ansible-galaxy collection install`, how is a specific version range requested for a collection?', 'Ansible', 'Version Pinning', 'mcq');
VALUES ('a38913a7-ef13-43cc-a508-23cf981d9986', 'f9ceb413-c6d9-40e8-bf71-be30bf3ee357', 'ansible-galaxy collection install accepts a version range identifier appended to the collection name (e.g. name:>=X,<Y), and production use is generally recommended to pin versions this way.', 'Ansible Content Collections — FQCNs, ansible-galaxy collection install, requirements.yml — authored from docs.ansible.com''s collections user guide; verified via web search 2026-09-04.');

VALUES ('709935e3-8b0c-4a9b-aa63-08141f3d6390', 'bcc754bf-d1f5-43c2-9a6c-2950b40639f3', 5, 'A single requirements.yml file lists both `roles:` and `collections:` entries. What is true about installing from that one file?', 'Ansible', 'requirements.yml Structure', 'mcq');
VALUES ('709935e3-8b0c-4a9b-aa63-08141f3d6390', '7ec5bdac-e865-44b7-8851-2dac58cf5896', 'Even when both are listed in one requirements.yml, roles and collections are installed via their own respective ansible-galaxy subcommands pointed at the same file.', 'Ansible Content Collections — FQCNs, ansible-galaxy collection install, requirements.yml — authored from docs.ansible.com''s collections user guide; verified via web search 2026-09-04.');

VALUES ('81f46114-1d89-4a51-b90d-8ad1f4c2f43a', 'bcc754bf-d1f5-43c2-9a6c-2950b40639f3', 6, 'Besides Ansible Galaxy itself, which of the following are valid sources ansible-galaxy can install a collection from?', 'Ansible', 'Collection Sources', 'mcq');
VALUES ('81f46114-1d89-4a51-b90d-8ad1f4c2f43a', 'd954d50e-4aa2-41be-8551-c36f38ff475e', 'ansible-galaxy collection install supports Galaxy/Automation Hub, Git repositories, direct URLs, and local tarballs, giving flexibility for both connected and air-gapped/offline environments.', 'Ansible Content Collections — FQCNs, ansible-galaxy collection install, requirements.yml — authored from docs.ansible.com''s collections user guide; verified via web search 2026-09-04.');

VALUES ('fa40fbf8-68ba-4a12-95c4-29a454c59462', 'bcc754bf-d1f5-43c2-9a6c-2950b40639f3', 7, 'Running `ansible-galaxy collection install -r requirements.yml -p ./collections` does what differently from omitting `-p`?', 'Ansible', 'Collection Install Path', 'mcq');
VALUES ('fa40fbf8-68ba-4a12-95c4-29a454c59462', 'e7b7b385-be04-41b5-b4c4-ccba5d5c8713', '-p overrides the install destination, letting a project vendor its collections into a local, project-relative directory rather than the shared default path.', 'Ansible Content Collections — FQCNs, ansible-galaxy collection install, requirements.yml — authored from docs.ansible.com''s collections user guide; verified via web search 2026-09-04.');

VALUES ('84192c73-bf63-4e49-bc1a-a869b0cbb8e0', 'bcc754bf-d1f5-43c2-9a6c-2950b40639f3', 8, 'What is the key structural difference between an Ansible Collection and an Ansible Role?', 'Ansible', 'Collections vs. Roles', 'mcq');
VALUES ('84192c73-bf63-4e49-bc1a-a869b0cbb8e0', 'ce252aa7-8aa9-4981-ba11-11e63856c778', 'A Collection is the broader packaging format — it can contain modules, plugins, playbooks, and one or more roles; a Role is a narrower, single reusable automation unit that a collection commonly ships inside.', 'Ansible Content Collections — FQCNs, ansible-galaxy collection install, requirements.yml — authored from docs.ansible.com''s collections user guide; verified via web search 2026-09-04.');

VALUES ('f8ae77d0-5b95-4c8e-9142-1d069b690db3', 'bcc754bf-d1f5-43c2-9a6c-2950b40639f3', 9, 'Which command lets you browse the modules/plugins available inside collections already installed on the current control node?', 'Ansible', 'Discovering Collection Content', 'mcq');
VALUES ('f8ae77d0-5b95-4c8e-9142-1d069b690db3', '3a3adf79-3b69-4ec8-ade5-aeaceacf47b8', 'ansible-galaxy collection list enumerates installed collections and their versions; ansible-doc <FQCN> shows documentation for a specific module/plugin inside one.', 'Ansible Content Collections — FQCNs, ansible-galaxy collection install, requirements.yml — authored from docs.ansible.com''s collections user guide; verified via web search 2026-09-04.');

-- ── Section: Execution Environments (ansible-builder / ansible-runner) (10 questions) — Execution Environments — ansible-builder/ansible-runner definitions and workflow — authored from docs.ansible.com's Builder and Runner project documentation; verified via web search 2026-09-04. ──

VALUES ('8775b754-1b8a-4286-8c08-196e40921748', 'bcc754bf-d1f5-43c2-9a6c-2950b40639f3', 10, 'What is an Ansible Execution Environment (EE)?', 'Ansible', 'What an Execution Environment Is', 'mcq');
VALUES ('8775b754-1b8a-4286-8c08-196e40921748', '7d8d5114-43b2-445b-b5c4-e098ffe44998', 'An Execution Environment is a container image (OCI-compliant) that packages ansible-core plus the collections and dependencies a set of playbooks needs, so the automation runs the same way regardless of what''s installed on the host running it.', 'Execution Environments — ansible-builder/ansible-runner definitions and workflow — authored from docs.ansible.com''s Builder and Runner project documentation; verified via web search 2026-09-04.');

VALUES ('4a68a748-2de0-424d-9bfb-fc95ca24c3b9', 'bcc754bf-d1f5-43c2-9a6c-2950b40639f3', 11, 'What problem do Execution Environments solve compared to the traditional model of installing Ansible and all its collection dependencies directly on a bare-metal/VM control node?', 'Ansible', 'Why Execution Environments Exist', 'mcq');
VALUES ('4a68a748-2de0-424d-9bfb-fc95ca24c3b9', '419b85d3-2a1e-4ec8-a474-a61d982dcded', 'EEs solve dependency drift and ''works on my machine'' problems: the exact same container image (with pinned versions) can run identically in a developer''s environment, CI, and Automation Controller.', 'Execution Environments — ansible-builder/ansible-runner definitions and workflow — authored from docs.ansible.com''s Builder and Runner project documentation; verified via web search 2026-09-04.');

VALUES ('2e718c11-c59a-485e-99fb-2ff3ec328777', 'bcc754bf-d1f5-43c2-9a6c-2950b40639f3', 12, 'What does ansible-builder do?', 'Ansible', 'ansible-builder''s Role', 'mcq');
VALUES ('2e718c11-c59a-485e-99fb-2ff3ec328777', 'f949ecdd-d63d-4bdb-ad79-ab2e26090245', 'ansible-builder is the tool that constructs an EE image from an execution-environment definition file, resolving and layering in the specified collections, Python requirements, and system packages.', 'Execution Environments — ansible-builder/ansible-runner definitions and workflow — authored from docs.ansible.com''s Builder and Runner project documentation; verified via web search 2026-09-04.');

VALUES ('2edc0bea-2dbc-4b68-b27d-eee585f2345d', 'bcc754bf-d1f5-43c2-9a6c-2950b40639f3', 13, 'An ansible-builder execution-environment definition file''s `dependencies` section is used to specify:', 'Ansible', 'EE Definition File Sections', 'mcq');
VALUES ('2edc0bea-2dbc-4b68-b27d-eee585f2345d', '6cd2bb3c-66b4-4290-88db-cae74d6064e6', 'The dependencies section lists what gets installed into the built image: ansible-core/runner, Python requirements, system-level packages, and collections.', 'Execution Environments — ansible-builder/ansible-runner definitions and workflow — authored from docs.ansible.com''s Builder and Runner project documentation; verified via web search 2026-09-04.');

VALUES ('3fd28a8d-6b23-4485-a09c-5ae4fd02dca1', 'bcc754bf-d1f5-43c2-9a6c-2950b40639f3', 14, 'Which ansible-builder definition file section lets you specify default values for build arguments passed into the underlying container build process?', 'Ansible', 'EE Definition File Sections (2)', 'mcq');
VALUES ('3fd28a8d-6b23-4485-a09c-5ae4fd02dca1', '0bfb2ce3-13ff-4e29-8aa2-36d07e7350f7', 'build_arg_defaults specifies default values for build args as a dictionary, used during the underlying container image construction.', 'Execution Environments — ansible-builder/ansible-runner definitions and workflow — authored from docs.ansible.com''s Builder and Runner project documentation; verified via web search 2026-09-04.');

VALUES ('29d4a537-44fa-47cc-bc01-77ea46559cbf', 'bcc754bf-d1f5-43c2-9a6c-2950b40639f3', 15, 'What is ansible-runner''s role in the Execution Environment workflow?', 'Ansible', 'ansible-runner''s Role', 'mcq');
VALUES ('29d4a537-44fa-47cc-bc01-77ea46559cbf', 'cc7578bd-8650-41b7-b843-984a9270bb72', 'ansible-runner executes Ansible content inside the container runtime using a specified EE image — it''s the execution layer, while ansible-builder is the image-construction layer.', 'Execution Environments — ansible-builder/ansible-runner definitions and workflow — authored from docs.ansible.com''s Builder and Runner project documentation; verified via web search 2026-09-04.');

VALUES ('54b4c309-3210-4243-8312-15e63c5dac16', 'bcc754bf-d1f5-43c2-9a6c-2950b40639f3', 16, 'In an EE definition file, which top-level section specifies the base container image the new Execution Environment is built on top of?', 'Ansible', 'Base Image Selection', 'mcq');
VALUES ('54b4c309-3210-4243-8312-15e63c5dac16', 'a37126b8-d0ae-4db4-b70b-2c2c60a0c71b', 'The images section specifies the base parent container image for the execution environment build.', 'Execution Environments — ansible-builder/ansible-runner definitions and workflow — authored from docs.ansible.com''s Builder and Runner project documentation; verified via web search 2026-09-04.');

VALUES ('5dd61941-d879-44e8-860c-56ff250207e1', 'bcc754bf-d1f5-43c2-9a6c-2950b40639f3', 17, 'If a team needs to run a custom shell command (e.g. installing an internal CA certificate) partway through the EE image build, which definition file section is designed for that?', 'Ansible', 'Adding Custom Build Logic', 'mcq');
VALUES ('5dd61941-d879-44e8-860c-56ff250207e1', '2972cfd3-051d-4b14-90b4-d63fc4c1f9da', 'additional_build_steps lets you insert custom build commands at defined stages (e.g. prepend/append) of the image creation process.', 'Execution Environments — ansible-builder/ansible-runner definitions and workflow — authored from docs.ansible.com''s Builder and Runner project documentation; verified via web search 2026-09-04.');

VALUES ('04dc260e-ee58-47c2-9870-f2e2ec9231de', 'bcc754bf-d1f5-43c2-9a6c-2950b40639f3', 18, 'A playbook developed and tested against a given Execution Environment image is handed to a CI pipeline and, separately, to Automation Controller. What must be true for the playbook to behave identically in all three places?', 'Ansible', 'EE Portability', 'mcq');
VALUES ('04dc260e-ee58-47c2-9870-f2e2ec9231de', 'ce749a9d-daef-488d-9996-f7646dc5acda', 'EEs only guarantee consistency if the same image (same tag or, more strictly, the same digest) is actually used everywhere — a ''latest''-tag pull at different times can still drift.', 'Execution Environments — ansible-builder/ansible-runner definitions and workflow — authored from docs.ansible.com''s Builder and Runner project documentation; verified via web search 2026-09-04.');

VALUES ('6ea64fd5-1a0d-454b-abb1-a43b6afb1546', 'bcc754bf-d1f5-43c2-9a6c-2950b40639f3', 19, 'Before Execution Environments, what did a team typically have to do to keep a bare-metal Ansible control node''s collection/Python dependencies consistent across multiple team members'' machines?', 'Ansible', 'Traditional Control Node vs. EE', 'mcq');
VALUES ('6ea64fd5-1a0d-454b-abb1-a43b6afb1546', 'cd83ab2d-1d91-4f04-9b33-b7a26cb20b14', 'Without EEs, keeping a control node''s dependency set consistent across machines required manual or configuration-managed replication of the same installs — exactly the drift problem EEs are designed to remove.', 'Execution Environments — ansible-builder/ansible-runner definitions and workflow — authored from docs.ansible.com''s Builder and Runner project documentation; verified via web search 2026-09-04.');

-- ── Section: ansible-navigator Usage (19 questions) — ansible-navigator usage — subcommands, settings precedence, run modes, pull policy — authored from docs.ansible.com/projects/navigator documentation; verified via web search 2026-09-04. Confirmed no 'doctor' subcommand exists in the current documented CLI. ──

VALUES ('3c46f8e7-e871-4db8-8efc-8502b1466868', 'bcc754bf-d1f5-43c2-9a6c-2950b40639f3', 20, 'What is ansible-navigator?', 'Ansible', 'ansible-navigator Purpose', 'mcq');
VALUES ('3c46f8e7-e871-4db8-8efc-8502b1466868', 'cf25de44-3da6-490a-9b8b-451b77833793', 'ansible-navigator is Ansible''s TUI/CLI front end for running playbooks and exploring related content (inventory, docs, config), built with Execution Environment-based execution as its default model.', 'ansible-navigator usage — subcommands, settings precedence, run modes, pull policy — authored from docs.ansible.com/projects/navigator documentation; verified via web search 2026-09-04. Confirmed no ''doctor'' subcommand exists in the current documented CLI.');

VALUES ('9a4a4eaf-c1fd-4a7b-b43c-03afa155509d', 'bcc754bf-d1f5-43c2-9a6c-2950b40639f3', 21, 'Which ansible-navigator subcommand actually executes a playbook?', 'Ansible', 'ansible-navigator run', 'mcq');
VALUES ('9a4a4eaf-c1fd-4a7b-b43c-03afa155509d', '1ff53973-cb69-4b3f-93d0-9fb660eafdb0', '`ansible-navigator run <playbook>` is the subcommand that runs a playbook (inside an Execution Environment by default).', 'ansible-navigator usage — subcommands, settings precedence, run modes, pull policy — authored from docs.ansible.com/projects/navigator documentation; verified via web search 2026-09-04. Confirmed no ''doctor'' subcommand exists in the current documented CLI.');

VALUES ('82affb72-3787-492d-902f-7ada09507a03', 'bcc754bf-d1f5-43c2-9a6c-2950b40639f3', 22, 'What does the `ansible-navigator images` subcommand do?', 'Ansible', 'ansible-navigator images', 'mcq');
VALUES ('82affb72-3787-492d-902f-7ada09507a03', '6c1b23e7-1de9-4718-b193-7fe6ad2420f9', 'images lets you explore/inspect Execution Environment images already available locally or configured for use — not build or run anything.', 'ansible-navigator usage — subcommands, settings precedence, run modes, pull policy — authored from docs.ansible.com/projects/navigator documentation; verified via web search 2026-09-04. Confirmed no ''doctor'' subcommand exists in the current documented CLI.');

VALUES ('15f02913-94af-4682-8f51-350671702f01', 'bcc754bf-d1f5-43c2-9a6c-2950b40639f3', 23, 'What does the `ansible-navigator builder` subcommand do?', 'Ansible', 'ansible-navigator builder', 'mcq');
VALUES ('15f02913-94af-4682-8f51-350671702f01', '0668ef29-8338-432e-af54-cab95686a388', 'The builder subcommand''s documented purpose is to build an Execution Environment (container image) — surfacing ansible-builder-style functionality directly through ansible-navigator.', 'ansible-navigator usage — subcommands, settings precedence, run modes, pull policy — authored from docs.ansible.com/projects/navigator documentation; verified via web search 2026-09-04. Confirmed no ''doctor'' subcommand exists in the current documented CLI.');

VALUES ('9c3b8344-a317-48ea-903f-8646b63b409b', 'bcc754bf-d1f5-43c2-9a6c-2950b40639f3', 24, 'What does the `ansible-navigator collections` subcommand let you do?', 'Ansible', 'ansible-navigator collections', 'mcq');
VALUES ('9c3b8344-a317-48ea-903f-8646b63b409b', 'cdd2cfea-53a1-4a7e-b2ef-138148d4e725', 'collections is an exploration subcommand — it lets you browse what collections are available/installed in the context ansible-navigator is using, not install or manage them.', 'ansible-navigator usage — subcommands, settings precedence, run modes, pull policy — authored from docs.ansible.com/projects/navigator documentation; verified via web search 2026-09-04. Confirmed no ''doctor'' subcommand exists in the current documented CLI.');

VALUES ('c6e02e5b-19bd-4269-855d-7c456b119f5d', 'bcc754bf-d1f5-43c2-9a6c-2950b40639f3', 25, 'A colleague claims RHCE candidates should memorize `ansible-navigator doctor` for diagnosing execution-environment problems. Based on the currently documented ansible-navigator subcommand list, is this accurate?', 'Ansible', 'Nonexistent Subcommand Check', 'mcq');
VALUES ('c6e02e5b-19bd-4269-855d-7c456b119f5d', '3553ae8f-9e27-49c8-9296-6e0e223302e9', 'There is no `doctor` subcommand in ansible-navigator''s documented CLI. The real subcommand set (per docs.ansible.com/projects/navigator/subcommands/) is welcome, run, exec, images, doc, config, collections, builder, replay, inventory, lint, and settings — ''doctor'' does not appear among them.', 'ansible-navigator usage — subcommands, settings precedence, run modes, pull policy — authored from docs.ansible.com/projects/navigator documentation; verified via web search 2026-09-04. Confirmed no ''doctor'' subcommand exists in the current documented CLI.');

VALUES ('757f31d2-c304-4114-9209-b14e3cc710b1', 'bcc754bf-d1f5-43c2-9a6c-2950b40639f3', 26, 'Running `ansible-navigator run site.yml --mode stdout` instead of the default interactive mode changes what?', 'Ansible', 'Interactive vs. stdout Mode', 'mcq');
VALUES ('757f31d2-c304-4114-9209-b14e3cc710b1', '62d3b1c6-bb3b-4719-bb93-6a4885af5aff', '--mode stdout prints results directly to the terminal (similar to ansible-playbook''s own output) rather than opening the interactive TUI, which is why it''s the mode typically used in CI/CD.', 'ansible-navigator usage — subcommands, settings precedence, run modes, pull policy — authored from docs.ansible.com/projects/navigator documentation; verified via web search 2026-09-04. Confirmed no ''doctor'' subcommand exists in the current documented CLI.');

VALUES ('7139fe90-c1e1-43a8-92b8-ecc7384fd15c', 'bcc754bf-d1f5-43c2-9a6c-2950b40639f3', 27, 'For a given ansible-navigator setting available via all three mechanisms, what is the correct precedence order from LOWEST to HIGHEST priority?', 'Ansible', 'Settings Precedence', 'mcq');
VALUES ('7139fe90-c1e1-43a8-92b8-ecc7384fd15c', 'f71a5a47-7ba5-4165-a273-f274bd8103bc', 'Precedence from lowest to highest is: built-in defaults -> settings file -> environment variables -> CLI parameters, with CLI flags always winning when a setting is specified in more than one place.', 'ansible-navigator usage — subcommands, settings precedence, run modes, pull policy — authored from docs.ansible.com/projects/navigator documentation; verified via web search 2026-09-04. Confirmed no ''doctor'' subcommand exists in the current documented CLI.');

VALUES ('f247d330-802c-4b6f-a78d-fa8c8b1e84b1', 'bcc754bf-d1f5-43c2-9a6c-2950b40639f3', 28, 'If ANSIBLE_NAVIGATOR_CONFIG is not set, where does ansible-navigator look for a settings file, and in what order?', 'Ansible', 'Settings File Discovery', 'mcq');
VALUES ('f247d330-802c-4b6f-a78d-fa8c8b1e84b1', '7d7111ad-0c8d-45d3-8e9a-9c48d8c1f23a', 'Absent an explicit ANSIBLE_NAVIGATOR_CONFIG path, ansible-navigator checks the current project directory first, then the home directory — the project-directory file takes precedence over the home-directory one.', 'ansible-navigator usage — subcommands, settings precedence, run modes, pull policy — authored from docs.ansible.com/projects/navigator documentation; verified via web search 2026-09-04. Confirmed no ''doctor'' subcommand exists in the current documented CLI.');

VALUES ('4b3bf1bb-256b-4415-897a-1e551e282461', 'bcc754bf-d1f5-43c2-9a6c-2950b40639f3', 29, 'What does `--pull-policy missing` (short form `--pp missing`) do when ansible-navigator needs an Execution Environment image?', 'Ansible', 'Pull Policy', 'mcq');
VALUES ('4b3bf1bb-256b-4415-897a-1e551e282461', 'ab7d0100-1d94-4cab-8c7f-9edee41c8009', 'The `missing` pull policy only triggers a pull when the image isn''t already present locally, distinct from `always` (always re-pull), `never` (never pull), and `tag` (re-pull only if the tag is ''latest'').', 'ansible-navigator usage — subcommands, settings precedence, run modes, pull policy — authored from docs.ansible.com/projects/navigator documentation; verified via web search 2026-09-04. Confirmed no ''doctor'' subcommand exists in the current documented CLI.');

VALUES ('e43a9e37-44de-43a4-8c70-41982bfcdf63', 'bcc754bf-d1f5-43c2-9a6c-2950b40639f3', 30, 'What does the `ansible-navigator config` subcommand let you review?', 'Ansible', 'ansible-navigator config', 'mcq');
VALUES ('e43a9e37-44de-43a4-8c70-41982bfcdf63', '910c8714-c677-4612-9c74-e8688fe2278c', 'config lets you explore the current Ansible configuration (the ansible.cfg-driven settings), distinct from `settings`, which reviews ansible-navigator''s own settings.', 'ansible-navigator usage — subcommands, settings precedence, run modes, pull policy — authored from docs.ansible.com/projects/navigator documentation; verified via web search 2026-09-04. Confirmed no ''doctor'' subcommand exists in the current documented CLI.');

VALUES ('ad515323-6e49-4d81-b70d-977c942959da', 'bcc754bf-d1f5-43c2-9a6c-2950b40639f3', 31, 'What is the distinction between the `ansible-navigator settings` subcommand and the `ansible-navigator config` subcommand?', 'Ansible', 'ansible-navigator settings vs. config', 'mcq');
VALUES ('ad515323-6e49-4d81-b70d-977c942959da', '7ec89d2b-5aeb-4f6d-b024-211c0c62376d', 'settings surfaces ansible-navigator''s own configuration state; config surfaces the separate, underlying Ansible (ansible.cfg) configuration — two different configuration layers.', 'ansible-navigator usage — subcommands, settings precedence, run modes, pull policy — authored from docs.ansible.com/projects/navigator documentation; verified via web search 2026-09-04. Confirmed no ''doctor'' subcommand exists in the current documented CLI.');

VALUES ('67218d88-66c7-464e-9c6f-ef4a524286a5', 'bcc754bf-d1f5-43c2-9a6c-2950b40639f3', 32, 'What does `ansible-navigator doc <fqcn>` do?', 'Ansible', 'ansible-navigator doc', 'mcq');
VALUES ('67218d88-66c7-464e-9c6f-ef4a524286a5', 'e29ac17e-6b02-4866-a0e2-8d93fb9ba56c', 'doc reviews documentation for a module or plugin — the navigator-integrated equivalent of running `ansible-doc` directly.', 'ansible-navigator usage — subcommands, settings precedence, run modes, pull policy — authored from docs.ansible.com/projects/navigator documentation; verified via web search 2026-09-04. Confirmed no ''doctor'' subcommand exists in the current documented CLI.');

VALUES ('51ce929a-d469-489c-b6db-1a1975a7e6ba', 'bcc754bf-d1f5-43c2-9a6c-2950b40639f3', 33, 'How does `ansible-navigator exec` differ from `ansible-navigator run`?', 'Ansible', 'ansible-navigator exec', 'mcq');
VALUES ('51ce929a-d469-489c-b6db-1a1975a7e6ba', '5f1b094d-fb96-4c4b-b993-8807e57d30b3', 'exec runs a given command within an Execution Environment (useful for debugging what''s actually inside the EE, e.g. checking installed packages), whereas run specifically executes a playbook.', 'ansible-navigator usage — subcommands, settings precedence, run modes, pull policy — authored from docs.ansible.com/projects/navigator documentation; verified via web search 2026-09-04. Confirmed no ''doctor'' subcommand exists in the current documented CLI.');

VALUES ('be399bf4-62b9-4feb-b29c-d183b1dc364a', 'bcc754bf-d1f5-43c2-9a6c-2950b40639f3', 34, 'What is the purpose of the `ansible-navigator inventory` subcommand?', 'Ansible', 'ansible-navigator inventory', 'mcq');
VALUES ('be399bf4-62b9-4feb-b29c-d183b1dc364a', '9ba67edd-c519-4625-a8c0-eb75ac85d292', 'inventory lets you explore an inventory''s structure (groups, hosts, variables) interactively, useful for verifying inventory content before a run.', 'ansible-navigator usage — subcommands, settings precedence, run modes, pull policy — authored from docs.ansible.com/projects/navigator documentation; verified via web search 2026-09-04. Confirmed no ''doctor'' subcommand exists in the current documented CLI.');

VALUES ('2a53841b-86bc-4f94-9ff4-5f08bbd417e0', 'bcc754bf-d1f5-43c2-9a6c-2950b40639f3', 35, 'What does `ansible-navigator replay` let you do?', 'Ansible', 'ansible-navigator replay', 'mcq');
VALUES ('2a53841b-86bc-4f94-9ff4-5f08bbd417e0', '8e8323f4-6d46-43a5-bb09-aba0e10b7cb7', 'replay opens a previous run''s saved playbook artifact for exploration in the TUI, letting you review what happened without touching real infrastructure again.', 'ansible-navigator usage — subcommands, settings precedence, run modes, pull policy — authored from docs.ansible.com/projects/navigator documentation; verified via web search 2026-09-04. Confirmed no ''doctor'' subcommand exists in the current documented CLI.');

VALUES ('63a1b388-656b-43d2-bd2b-6d88332e2818', 'bcc754bf-d1f5-43c2-9a6c-2950b40639f3', 36, 'What does the `ansible-navigator lint` subcommand do?', 'Ansible', 'ansible-navigator lint', 'mcq');
VALUES ('63a1b388-656b-43d2-bd2b-6d88332e2818', '4df4a2f9-5f37-430e-b38c-cb3d5fb3950e', 'lint checks a file or directory for common errors/issues (an ansible-lint-style pass) surfaced through the navigator CLI/TUI.', 'ansible-navigator usage — subcommands, settings precedence, run modes, pull policy — authored from docs.ansible.com/projects/navigator documentation; verified via web search 2026-09-04. Confirmed no ''doctor'' subcommand exists in the current documented CLI.');

VALUES ('6ca3e1b8-83d0-4afd-8e74-41cfa15f4a74', 'bcc754bf-d1f5-43c2-9a6c-2950b40639f3', 37, 'Why is ansible-navigator designed around Execution Environments as its default execution model, rather than running directly against whatever is installed on the local control node?', 'Ansible', 'Why EE-First Matters for Navigator', 'mcq');
VALUES ('6ca3e1b8-83d0-4afd-8e74-41cfa15f4a74', '5f596c92-76ac-476b-9e71-015164a9ebbf', 'ansible-navigator''s EE-first design ties directly back to why EEs exist: it makes the exact dependency set explicit and portable, rather than implicitly depending on the local control node''s ad hoc installs (navigator does support a --execution-environment false local-execution mode, but EE-based execution is the intended default).', 'ansible-navigator usage — subcommands, settings precedence, run modes, pull policy — authored from docs.ansible.com/projects/navigator documentation; verified via web search 2026-09-04. Confirmed no ''doctor'' subcommand exists in the current documented CLI.');

VALUES ('92a44c5c-d84f-40a1-b757-edb2771541bb', 'bcc754bf-d1f5-43c2-9a6c-2950b40639f3', 38, 'When running `ansible-navigator doc ansible.posix.firewalld`, where does navigator resolve that module''s documentation from?', 'Ansible', 'Content Collections in Navigator''s doc View', 'mcq');
VALUES ('92a44c5c-d84f-40a1-b757-edb2771541bb', 'da6f44a2-b6f8-40f3-a408-08465ac9b343', 'doc resolves a module/plugin''s documentation from wherever that collection actually lives for the current run context — the configured EE image''s installed collections, or the local install path when running without an EE.', 'ansible-navigator usage — subcommands, settings precedence, run modes, pull policy — authored from docs.ansible.com/projects/navigator documentation; verified via web search 2026-09-04. Confirmed no ''doctor'' subcommand exists in the current documented CLI.');
